    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="instruction-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">FMLS (indexed)</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Floating-point fused multiply-subtract by indexed element</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction multiplies all floating-point elements within each 128-bit
segment of the first source vector by the specified element in
the corresponding second source vector segment.  The products are then destructively subtracted without intermediate rounding from the corresponding
elements of the addend and destination vector.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">The elements within the second source vector are specified using
an immediate index that selects the same element position within
each 128-bit vector segment. The index range is from 0 to
one less than the number of elements per 128-bit segment.
This instruction is unpredicated.</p>
    
    <p class="desc">
      It has encodings from 3 classes:
      <a href="#iclass_half_precision">Half-precision</a>
      , 
      <a href="#iclass_single_precision">Single-precision</a>
       and 
      <a href="#iclass_double_precision">Double-precision</a>
    </p>
